      "message": "\u003e I\u0027d agree with you, but since the true behavior of the chip seems to be setting that bit, I may have to emulate that behavior later. Maybe I also need to make this unit test more explicit that we are verifying the driver forces that bit to be set regardless of expected behavior of the device (which may be a wrong requirement) during dead battery boot. But I\u0027m happy to remove the interception until it\u0027s absolutely necessary. Can you confirm I should do that?\n\nThe main thing that I want for this CL is a comment explaining what behavior it\u0027s verifying.\n\nI\u0027d like it if emulator modeled the chip accurately, and the test was based on the emulator state. But if those are the only things holding up this CL chain, they can go in a follow-up CL.\n\n\u003e I now think that regardless if we remove this code we should make a tracking bug for removing this seeming redundant code. It\u0027s obviously not high priority, but it does seem like something we\u0027d want tracked. Do agree? If so, I can make it and insert the todo.\n\nI\u0027d ask Aseda, since he wrote it. Whether you do that over chat or by filing a bug and CCing him is a matter of personal style.",
